Work backlog item PL-48, candidate PL48-03: src/features/projects-dashboard/ui/components/ProjectCard.tsx
It ranks 35 of 40 tests redundant (88%) over 31 mutable decisions.

READ scripts/overnight/PL48.md FIRST. It carries the evidence for every rule below and does
not change between candidates.

THE RANKING IS A READING ORDER, NOT A WORKLIST. A high ratio means "many tests, few
decisions", which happens both when a suite repeats itself AND when a module simply has
little to decide. Consolidation does NOT move the metric — measured. The payoff is what
reading finds.

DONE is either of these, and the second is a complete success:
  (a) real repetition -> converted to it.each tables, exact assertions, ratchet held
  (b) arithmetic -> recorded on PL-48 with the reason, nothing changed

FIRST: read the module. Count its actual decisions. A thin factory, a constants file or an
already-table-driven suite explains the ratio by itself — say so and stop.

IF IT IS REAL REPETITION:
  - rows are the INPUTS; keep each test's name as the row LABEL when it carries a reason
  - assert EXACT values, derived from the source, never `not.toContain` or `toBeDefined`
    where the exact result is knowable
  - do NOT target the minimal covering set — a case worth naming is worth keeping

WHILE READING, these are the finds that matter more than the tidying: an assertion that
cannot fail, an assertion too weak to catch a mutant, a decision nothing covers, a test whose
subject is declared in another module, dead code with no importer. Fix what you find and say
so in the commit. A defect in src/ may be fixed — say which.

CHECK, SCOPED: the module's suites, `npx tsc --noEmit`, `npm run typecheck:tests`, eslint on
changed files, and `npm run validate:test-file-sizes`. Exit codes in variables, never read
through a pipe. Then re-measure:
  rm -f reports/mutation/focus-incremental.json
  node scripts/focusModule.mjs src/features/projects-dashboard/ui/components/ProjectCard.tsx
  npx stryker run stryker.focus.config.json > /tmp/focus.txt 2>&1   (wait on `Done in`)
  node scripts/checkMutationBaseline.mjs --report reports/mutation/focus.json
The open-gap count must not RISE. If the score moves, say why in the commit.

RULES. Stay on the work branch; never checkout or merge develop. One commit for this
candidate, `Backlog: PL-48` trailer, explicit pathspec (`git commit -- <paths>`), never bare
`git commit` or `-a`. No cloud writes. No attribution trailers. Commit only on a green check.

If a rename or a new suite forms a test family, `tests/sop/test-family-setup.test.ts` needs a
shared .testUtils — and it reads GIT-TRACKED files, so `git add` before trusting it.

FINISH with two or three plain sentences: which of (a) or (b), what changed, what reading
found.
